From: 1Pro-L4R8 <hoangquocvietbk2.13@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 19:54:10 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Require OPERATE on SYSTEM for FILES()

FILES() had no privilege of its own (upstream #79980, #80233): any user who
could log in read and wrote object storage through it, with no table
privilege, column mask or row filter, and with
"aws.s3.use_instance_profile" through the BE's own cloud identity, which can
reach the data files of every table.

Every use (SELECT ... FROM FILES, INSERT INTO FILES, DESC FILES) now needs
the OPERATE privilege on SYSTEM, refused with error 5211 otherwise.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
